  "abstract_interpretations": {
    "amsgrad": "The authors diagnose failures of exponential-moment optimizers, construct counterexamples, and propose variants with longer gradient memory. This is conditional theory plus selected experiments, not evidence of universal failure or superiority.",
    "adafactor": "The paper proposes factored moment state, update clipping, changing decay and parameter scaling, with Transformer translation experiments. The record retains mechanism evidence without importing benchmark claims.",
    "astar": "The paper incorporates domain heuristics into formal graph search and studies optimality properties. Algorithm mechanics are curated separately from broader efficiency claims and later corrections.",
    "strips": "The paper presents a planner combining predicate-calculus world models, theorem proving and means–ends analysis; the curated concept is its procedure, not all later representations sharing the name."
  },
